	<Item Name="title" Type="String">CRISPR screen for interferon-alpha inducible inhibitors of yellow fever virus replication</Item>
	<Item Name="summary" Type="String">Host cells produce interferon (IFN) in response to viral infections. Secreted interferon results in the transcription and production of hundreds of interferon-stimulated genes (ISGs). A genome-wide CRISPR screen using IFN alpha-treated Huh7.5 cells was performed to determine which ISGs were required in order for host cells to suppress yellow fever virus (YFV) infection.</Item>
